# Agent bus — coordination between agents working this repo

Append-only channel for every agent (and human) working this repository, carried
by git. `AGENT_BUS.md merge=union` in `.gitattributes` makes concurrent appends
from different branches combine instead of conflicting. Append new entries at
the END of the file, never at the top: union merge relies on it.

## Before you start: read the digest, not this file

```bash
./manage.sh bus --digest        # open claims + the last 15 entries
./manage.sh bus --digest --n 40 # more history
```

The digest is what a task needs. A bus grows without bound; reading all of it
every task costs more tokens than the task.

## Protocol

1. **Pull first** so you see the others' latest entries and code.
2. **Claim before you edit.** Append one line and push it before starting:
   `- [<UTC ISO-8601>Z] **<agent>**: CLAIM <version or area> — <what you are doing>`
3. **Respect open claims.** Never edit what another agent holds; pick other work
   or wait. `./manage.sh bus` lists open and expired leases.
4. **Release when done:** `- [<ts>Z] **<agent>**: RELEASE <same key> — <summary>`.
5. **Coordinate here, not in code comments.**

Leases: a claim expires after 72h (`SUBSTRATE_CLAIM_TTL_HOURS`). Extend it with
`HEARTBEAT <key>`; take over an expired one with `RECLAIM <key> — <why>`. Only
lines in exactly the format above are read; `./manage.sh bus` warns about any
claim-shaped line it cannot parse rather than ignoring it.

